---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
import { url } from '../lib';
---

<Layout
  title="Player Support | Encrypted Cat Games"
  description="Get help with The Cradle games, report a bug, or contact Encrypted Cat Games."
>
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Player support</p>
    <h1>A light when you need it.</h1>
    <p>Help with The Cradle: Episode 01 and The Cradle: Trick-or-Treat.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container support-grid section">
    <div>
      <h2>Before you send a signal.</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>How do I play on iPhone or iPad?</summary>
          <p>
            Open the game’s itch.io page in Safari. For Episode 01 on iPhone,
            use Share → Add to Home Screen, then launch from the new icon to
            play without browser bars. On iPad, use the game’s full-screen
            button. Rotate your device to landscape.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href={url('games/')}>
            Find your game
          </a>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>The game runs slowly or won’t load.</summary>
          <p>
            Try a current browser, close other tabs, and reload the game. In
            Episode 01, lower graphics quality in Settings. If it still fails,
            send us your device model, operating system, browser version, and
            the point where loading stops.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where can I adjust controls and comfort settings?</summary>
          <p>
            Episode 01 includes graphics, brightness, sensitivity, key
            rebinding, and interface size settings. Its Comfort settings offer
            options for a more comfortable experience. Headphones are
            recommended; you can also use subtitles.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I report a bug?</summary>
          <p>
            Tell us which game you played, your device and operating system,
            browser or app version, what you expected, and what happened
            instead. Include steps to reproduce and any error text. Avoid
            including passwords or personal account information.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where are the iPhone and iPad App Store versions?</summary>
          <p>
            App Store links will appear on the game pages when available. The
            current game pages link to itch.io. For questions about native
            releases, contact us below.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="support-form">
      <h2>Contact support.</h2>
      <p>Tell us what happened. We’ll reply to the email you provide.</p>
      <ContactForm />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
